"{\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"I’d investigate the Hong Kong connection first: it pairs a shorter journey with stronger reported seat availability than the earlier-arriving Taiwan option. The tradeoff is a later Bangkok arrival.\"},{\"k\":\"p\",\"r\":\"J14@2027-01-15T23:15-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T09:50\",\"n\":\"Hong Kong connection\",\"v\":\"This Aeroplan economy award via HKG is the more practical balance against the Taiwan alternative: it reports 9 seats and a 70-minute award connection. It shows 65,000 points plus CAD 107.40 in taxes/fees, but the quote scope is unknown. Its drawback is arriving later in Bangkok; the reported itinerary still has a connection.\"},{\"k\":\"p\",\"r\":\"J7@2027-01-15T12:00-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T01:25\",\"n\":\"Earlier Taiwan arrival\",\"v\":\"Choose this Aeroplan economy award via TPE if arriving earlier matters most; it reaches Bangkok at 01:25 and has a 4-hour-30-minute award connection. The cost is a longer journey, with only 1 reported seat. It also shows 65,000 points plus CAD 116.50 in taxes/fees, with unknown quote scope.\"},{\"k\":\"x\",\"r\":\"T09\"},{\"k\":\"b\",\"r\":\"C1@2027-01-15T09:40-08:00/SFO>BKK\",\"n\":\"Cash baseline\",\"v\":\"The search returned a USD 440 one-stop Singapore Airlines itinerary via SIN. This is origin-to-destination cash context, not an all-in award comparison: its price scope is unknown, and the search’s 1 returned traveler is not evidence that the quoted amount is per traveler.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"Both award records are assembled itineraries, not confirmed bookings or proof of current availability. Award points and fee quote scopes are unknown; the separate cash quote’s scope is also unknown. Search coverage was partial, and results may not be real-time, so verify current itinerary details and prices with the booking providers before deciding.\"}]}"
